course: dictionary
lesson: 5488
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Latin has more than one meaning, so context tells you which one you need. Look at the words around it. «Millions of immigrants came to America from Europe, Asia and Latin America» shows that Latin here names a place, not a language.
explain: As a noun, Latin is the language of the ancient Romans. «Latin, the old language of Rome and of European learning, keeps giving words too» means the language itself. Ask yourself: is Latin a thing here, or is it describing something?
explain: As an adjective, Latin describes something, as in «Latin music» or «Latin names». Test your meaning: if you swap in "from Latin America" and the sentence still makes sense, you have got it.
fact: Latin is the language of the ancient Romans.
fact: Latin is no longer anyone's first language, but it is still studied and used in science and law.
fact: Spanish, Portuguese, Italian and French come from Latin, so they are called Latin languages.
fact: «Latin America» means the countries of Mexico, Central America and South America.
fact: Many English words come from Latin, such as «video», «audio» and «bus», and «am» comes from «ante meridiem».
exercise: «Latin, the old language of Rome, keeps giving words to English.» What is Latin in this sentence? | *A language | A kind of music | A place to visit | A country
exercise: «Latin music» uses Latin as what kind of word? | A noun, a name for a thing | A country | *An adjective, a describing word | A verb, a doing word
exercise: What does «am» come from? | A video game name | *Latin: «ante meridiem», meaning before midday | A country in Europe
test: What does «Latin America» mean? | *Mexico, Central America and South America | The city of New York | Only the Statue of Liberty | Only ancient Rome
test: «The Latin alphabet, which English uses» tells us English uses which alphabet? | Chinese | Greek | Arabic | *The Latin alphabet
exam: Priya says Latin is a language nobody uses at all. What is the best answer? | Yes, nobody uses it anywhere, so it is dead and has no words left | No, it is a verb that means to speak | Yes, it is only a country | *No, it is still studied and used in science and law, and it gives English words like «video»
